Hillsdale was a very good place to be in  late 50s  my brother attended Hillsdale and was a  good athlete there the previous few  years and he knew all the coaches and I  think he put a good word in for me to  get a scholarship so I had moved up  there in August for early football  practice and the rest is history  it probably impressed the coaches in the  four years I was there I never missed  the practice and sometimes that's not  easy to do especially in football I  think I got on this good side of Coach  waters and the other coaches because I  was willing to sacrifice and no matter  what I was gonna make practice and I  never missed a game and in my senior  year we went to the mineral bowl in Cape  Girardeau Missouri we wound up winning  which is I think the only bowl game that  Hillsdale College ever won and I'm proud  of the fact that I was on that team I  wasn't the best student in the world but  I was able to do a decent job my first  two years I was a a seed B student my  last two years and I credit my wife now  Peggy because I become a be a student  with her prodding and and making sure  that I kept the right things in order  which was academics obviously I met her  at kindergarten they're here at new  Troy's oh it's been quite a relationship  that we've had  and knowing her since she was 4 years  old in kindergarten I decided to the  closest thing I could get staying in  athletics was to go into coaching I went  into the high school ranks and I coached  a total of 48 years the last 10 being an  assistant to my son who was at Lake  Michigan College so a majority of my  time the 38 years was at high school and  most of those were at River Valley high  school I was very fortunate to have  great teams great players and players  who sacrifice for the good of the team  and as a result I was a beneficiary of  many good experiences we were over the  years with very successful eight or nine  districts and five or six regionals we  went to the Final Four four times that  first year in 1979 we won the  championship going to the Final Four  meant the first three years we played at  Chrysler arena and believe me that was a  thrill from a little little country boy  here in Sawyer Michigan I have  tremendous support from my family my  four sons our daughter-in-laws my  grandkids unbelievable support and when  the times get tough their support even  grows believe me Peggy and I appreciate  that a great deal  [Music]  you  [Music]
 

